 'DO: (1) write migrations/2026-11-06-spend-governor-cached-pricing.sql with the header lines -- APPLY-BY: ci, -- DB: qnfo-audit, -- BACKUP: spend_governor_plan, a single-line -- Rollback: that recreates the old view text from migrations/2026-11-05-w2f-a-spend-governor-plan.sql, then DROP VIEW IF EXISTS v_spend_governor_plan and CREATE VIEW v_spend_governor_plan with the same columns, where for purpose ledger-rollup the alternative cost is (in_tok - cached_tok) * price_in + cached_tok * price_in * 0.1 + out_tok * price_out, with cached_tok summed from ai_spend_ledger rows for the same day window (caller qnfo-agents); other purposes unchanged. Never edit the merged migration. (2) extend migrations/spend-governor-plan.test.mjs (fixture tables ai_call_counters, cf_model_catalog, model_ab_runs, plus ai_spend_ledger) to prove a ledger-rollup row with 25 percent cached input now qualifies and an uncached one does not. (3) run node --no-warnings migrations/spend-governor-plan.test.mjs and python scripts/apply_migrations.py --check on the new file.' || char(10) ||
