INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT 'AI-METER-KIMI-1: the qnfo-ai binding wrapper skips its ai_call_counters write while the D1 breaker is open, so calls in an overload window are invisible (candidate for the kimi-k2.6 unattributed neurons)',
 'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-ai/worker.js' || char(10) ||
 'code-anchor: function d1AttrWriteSkip() { return Date.now() < __d1OverloadedUntil; }' || char(10) ||
 'code-probe: {"paths": ["qnfo-ai/worker.js"], "contains": "AI-METER-KIMI-1"}' || char(10) || char(10) ||
 'Charter pillar cost (program QNFO.INFRA), roadmap RM-ANALYTICS-ENGINE-METERS-1 (row 56), follow-up of agent_issues 1001927. Cold-start brief:' || char(10) ||
 'THE HOLE: v_ai_meter_vs_counters for 2026-11-04, model @cf/moonshotai/kimi-k2.6: Cloudflare meter 509,889 neurons and 1,206 requests, ai_call_counters 118,745 neurons and 191 calls, so 391,144 neurons and about 1,015 requests are unattributed; AI Gateway logs for kimi-k2.6 are empty (so they are Workers AI binding calls); the attributed callers are q08-signal-engine, qnfo-gateway, errata-hub and qnfo-ai-search.' || char(10) ||
 'HYPOTHESIS TO TEST FIRST (not proven): qnfo-ai routes kimi-k2.6 chat through its own Workers AI binding wrapper, and in that wrapper (the finally block near line 111 of qnfo-ai/worker.js) the counter write is guarded by !d1AttrWriteSkip(): while the D1 overload breaker is open (60 s windows, d1-overload-breaker.test.mjs) the call is made and not counted. The new Analytics Engine point is written in spendRecord only, which that wrapper path does not always reach.' || char(10) ||
 'DO: (1) measure: after 2026-11-06 00:00Z read, per UTC hour of 2026-11-06, kimi-k2.6 meter requests (ai_meter_model_daily has days only; use the Cloudflare GraphQL aiInferenceAdaptiveGroups by hour, as scripts/cost_ledger.py does) against ai_call_counters + ai_meter_ae_daily calls for kimi-k2.6, and against the hours where cloud_ops_events or the D1 breaker log show an overload; write the share explained into this issue. (2) if the unattributed hours are the overload hours: in the wrapper finally block, when d1AttrWriteSkip() is true, call aiMeterWrite(env, aiMeterPoint(...)) with the wrapper provider workers-ai, the model, the caller from env.__spendCaller and the usage tokens, so the call is counted in Analytics Engine even when D1 is skipped; mark the code with the id AI-METER-KIMI-1 in a comment (the code-probe reads it); test in qnfo-ai/ai-meter-ae.test.mjs (a wrapper call with the breaker open writes one point and no counter row); bump with python scripts/worker_release.py bump qnfo-ai; keep deployed-current.worker.js identical. (3) if the hours do not match, record the measurement here and name the next suspect (a worker that calls the binding without __aiAttrEnv: node scripts/ai_call_paths_audit.mjs lists them, and today it finds none, so look at callers that pass a different binding name or run before the wrapper is installed).' || char(10) ||
 'Definition of done: the measurement is written on this issue; either the AI-METER-KIMI-1 change is merged and deployed (qnfo-ai /health shows the new version) and the next complete day shows kimi-k2.6 attributed_pct in v_ai_meter_vs_counters above 60 (was 23.3 on 2026-11-04), or the measurement names the real cause and a new issue with a code-task carries it; recorded in issue_triage.close_evidence.',
 'session:w2f-a', 'reliability', 'medium', 'open', CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000, CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'AI-METER-KIMI-1:%' AND status = 'open');
